<title>AUSTRALIA: National Mutual chairman to retire.</title>
<headline>National Mutual chairman to retire.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Mutual Holdings Ltd Chairman Athol Lapthorne is to retire in 1997 and would be replaced by current deputy chairman Dean Wills, Lapthorne said.</p>
<p>Lapthorne, 69, told the company's annual meeting he was approaching the age of 70 and &quot;the time is right for me to retire.&quot;</p>
<p>National Mutual gave no timing for Lapthorne's retirement but said Wills would take up the position later this year.  </p>
<p>Wills, 63, is also chairman of Coca-Cola Amatil Ltd as well as a director of John Fairfax Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>Director Rick Allert, who's also chairman of Southcorp Holdings, is to become National Mutual's new deputy chairman.</p>
<p>National Mutual is 51 percent owned by French insurance group Axa SA.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne Bureau 61-3 9286-1421</p>
